# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root .gitignore
#
# PHASE 0 (step 0.1): before this phase the file only contained ".env".
# Each service already has its own .gitignore, but folders that live directly
# in the repo root (Integration-tests/, .idea/, docs/ ...) were not covered,
# so compiled classes and IDE settings ended up in Git.
#
# Rule of thumb: commit SOURCE, never things that can be GENERATED
# (build output, IDE caches, local secrets).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local secrets (DB passwords, JWT secret, later Auth0 credentials).
# Never commit them; every developer / CI system provides its own.
.env

# Maven build output of ANY module (also Integration-tests/, which has no own .gitignore).
# It is recreated by every "mvn package", so committing it only causes merge conflicts.
target/

# IntelliJ IDEA project files: personal editor settings, request logs, cookies.
# They differ per machine and can contain tokens from the HTTP client.
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr

# VS Code settings
.vscode/

# Operating-system junk files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# PHASE 1 (step 1.0): personal Claude Code settings (e.g. permission to read .env).
# Shared settings live in .claude/settings.json and ARE committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
